{
  "dom_id": "step-q96118",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Given the singular value decomposition $A=UΣ{V}^{T},$ where $A$ is a $3\\times 5$ matrix, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $U$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix\n\nII. $U$ is an orthogonal matrix\n\nIII. $Σ$ is an orthogonal matrix",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that if  $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n- $Σ$ is a $m\\times n$ matrix with nonnegative elements on the main diagonal and zeroes outside the main diagonal,\n\n- $U$ is an orthogonal $m\\times m$ matrix,\n\n- $V$ is an orthogonal $n\\times n$ matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $A$ is a $3\\times 5$ matrix, $U$ must be a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the matrix $U$ in the singular value decomposition $UΣ{V}^{T}$ must be orthogonal.\n\n- Statement III is false. The matrix $Σ$ must be diagonal but not necessarily orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
